From 5f40f551bea3e26ed308f5e33ed481984b56ee4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ObeseCatLord <6099645+ObeseCatLord@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:32:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ga2: VU1 program generator (constant-folded shared step),
 flag/store rings, exact double flags

- The run() loop body is now VU1Interpreter::stepPair (ps2_vu1_step.inl) and
  instruction execution lives in ps2_vu1_exec.inl, both always-inline.
- ga2_vu1_gen turns VU1 code images (GA2_VU1CAP captures or GA2_VU1_DUMP
  images) into C++: one constexpr DecodedInstructionPair per executed pair,
  chunked dispatch, and calls to the same stepPair, so the compiler folds
  decode, stall checks, write masks and opcode switches while semantics stay
  identical by construction. Programs register by code-image hash; anything
  unknown or uncovered uses the interpreter. GA2_VU1JIT=0 disables.
- Flag and store queues are rings (fixed latency, committed exactly at the
  ready cycle, so issue order equals the old slot order).
- FMAC flag classification uses double, falling back to long double only
  when the double result is exactly FLT_MAX (the only case where the two can
  classify differently under round-to-zero).
- ga2_vu1_replay shares a capture reader with the generator.
- Replay of all captures: 0 mismatches; 97 us/run originally, 47 us now in the
  interpreter, 18 us with the generated program. The Zettai narration scene
  went from ~23 to 60 vsync/s.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
